course: dictionary
lesson: 1523
title: Centre: a point, a place, or a job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «The Milky Way is a barred spiral galaxy, with a bar of stars across its centre» uses centre for the middle point of something.
explain: «Urgent treatment centres and minor injury units deal with things like sprains, small cuts and minor burns» uses centre for a building or place set up for a special activity. The words treatment and injury are your clues. Check by swapping in a meaning: a place for treatment still makes sense.
explain: Centre can also be a verb, meaning to put something in the middle. «You stay balanced when the point where your weight is centred is above the area between your feet» means your weight is placed in the middle. Centre is the British spelling. In American English it is center, with the same meaning.
fact: Centre means the middle point or part of something.
fact: A centre is also a building or place used for a special activity, like a sports centre or health centre.
fact: The centre of attention is the person everyone is looking at.
fact: To centre something means to put it in the middle.
fact: In maths, the centre of a circle is the point the same distance from every point on the edge.
exercise: «The Milky Way is a barred spiral galaxy, with a bar of stars across its centre.» What does centre mean here? | *The middle point | A building for a special activity | The very edge of the galaxy | The person everyone is looking at
exercise: «Rescue centres take in lost or given-up animals.» What is a rescue centre? | A kind of animal that is lost | *A place set up for a special job, here looking after animals | The middle of a field | A person who finds lost things
exercise: Ella says the centre of attention means the middle of a room. What does it really mean? | *The person everyone is looking at | The quietest corner of the room | A seat at the back of the room | The spot in the room where the floor is strongest
test:
«You stay balanced when the point where your weight is centred is above the area between your feet.» What does centred mean here? | Spread out wide | *Placed in the middle, so you are balanced | Moved to one side | Made heavier
In maths, where is the centre of a circle? | At the edge of the circle | *The point the same distance from every point on the edge | Outside the circle, away from the edge | Anywhere along the line of the radius
exam:
Which is the American spelling of centre? | Centre | Centr | *Center | Senter
